  "id": "emotional-maturity",
  "term": "emotional maturity",
  "definition": "Emotional maturity is the psychological development that can occur as late adolescents grow older, marked in this study by becoming less neurotic, less anxious, less depressive, and more extraverted. It is described as part of broader social and emotional maturation linked to changes in brain systems involved in emotional processing and social cognition.",
